{
    desc => q{3F{char} finds the third occurrence of character backward},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/find_count_3F`

**3F{char}** with a count prefix finds the nth occurrence of the character backward. `$3Fa` starts from the end and finds the third 'a' going backward.

**Keys:** `$3Fa`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 10 (on 'a' at end of "abracadabra")
- Text: `abracadabra`

**after_3Fa.png**
- Cursor on the third 'a' from the right at col 7 (abrac**a**dabra)
- Counting backward from col 10: col 10 (1st), col 7 (2nd... wait, let me recount)
- From position 10: 'a'@10 (skip, current), 'a'@7 (1st back), 'a'@5 (2nd back), 'a'@3 (3rd back)
- Cursor on 'a' at col 3
- Text unchanged
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('$3Fa');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_3Fa');
    },
}
__DATA__
abracadabra
